/-!
# The surjection from the presented third Conway group onto its ATLAS model

`TauCeti.Sporadic.Co3` is the degree-276 permutation model generated by the two ATLAS permutations
`Co3.a` and `Co3.b`, while `TauCeti.SporadicName.Co3.Group` is the group defined by Đoković's
Coxeter-type presentation (13.1) on seven involutions `a, b, c, d, e, f, g` with twenty-four
defining relators.

To realize this presentation inside `Co3`, note that in presentation (13.1) the fifth involution
`e` commutes with `a, c, g` directly and hence also with `f = (ag)³` and `b = a(abc)c` via
`e = (abc)³`, so `⟨a, b, c, e, f, g⟩` centralizes `e`. Sending `e` to the centralizer-defining
involution `Co3.imageE = Co3.b ^ 2`, we choose involutions `Co3.imageA`, `Co3.imageB`,
`Co3.imageC`, `Co3.imageF`, and `Co3.imageG` in `C_{Co3}(Co3.b ^ 2)` satisfying the `2 · Sp₆(2)`
sub-presentation, and then choose `Co3.imageD` commuting with `Co3.imageA`, `Co3.imageB`, and
`Co3.imageG` such that `(imageC * imageD) ^ 3 = (imageD * imageE) ^ 3 = 1`.

Each of the seven involutions is exposed with its explicit `12 × 23` forward-image table so that
all twenty-four relator checks evaluate directly in the kernel. Explicit words in `Co3.a` and
`Co3.b` place every presentation image in `Co3`, while explicit words for `Co3.b` and `Co3.a` in
those seven involutions show that they generate the entire model `Co3`. Extending the assignment
via `TauCeti.GroupPresentation.homEquiv` and
`TauCeti.GroupPresentation.exists_surjective_of_closure_range_eq` yields the surjection
`TauCeti.Sporadic.exists_surjective_Co3` and the nontriviality of `TauCeti.SporadicName.Co3.Group`.
No order or simplicity assertion is made here.

## Main declarations

* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Co3.imageA` through `TauCeti.Sporadic.Co3.imageG`: the seven involutions in
  `Equiv.Perm (Fin 276)` realizing Đoković's generators.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Co3.presentationImage`: the generator assignment for `SporadicName.Co3`.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Co3.lift_presentationImage_toFreeGroup_eq_one`: all twenty-four transcribed
  relators of `Co₃` evaluate to `1` at `presentationImage`.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Co3.closure_range_presentationImage`: the seven images generate `Co3`.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Co3.presentationHom`: the induced homomorphism from `SporadicName.Co3.Group`
  to `Equiv.Perm (Fin 276)`, with range `Co3`.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.exists_surjective_Co3`: `SporadicName.Co3.Group` surjects onto `Co3`.

## References

* D. Ž. Đoković, *Presentations of some finite simple groups*, J. Austral. Math. Soc. Ser. A
  **45** (1988), 143--168, presentation (13.1), p. 162,
  <https://doi.org/10.1017/S1446788700030068>.
* R. A. Wilson, R. A. Parker, J. N. Bray et al., *ATLAS of Finite Group Representations*,
  version 3, representation `Co3G1-p276B0`.
-/

